WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.274
Oxford Bookworms. Starter.
 
00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:10.048
The Girl with Red Hair. By Christine Lindop.
 
00:00:10.108 --> 00:00:39.900
Published and Copyright Oxford University Press 2009. Read by Wayne Forrester.
 
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.140
Chapter 1. Wow!

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.695
My name is Mark Sellers.

00:00:51.755 --> 00:01:01.133
I'm 22 years old and I work in security in Mason's store.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:18.010
You can get everything here, books, TVs, hats, flowers, sandwiches, beds, bicycles.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:23.135
It's interesting work and I like it.

00:01:23.195 --> 00:01:35.978
Sometimes I walk around in the store and sometimes I work in the office.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:44.704
Leon and Shami work in security too.

00:01:44.764 --> 00:01:48.245
I like working with them.

00:01:48.305 --> 00:01:53.556
Look at this woman, Leon says.

00:01:53.616 --> 00:01:57.597
Which hat is best for her?

00:01:57.657 --> 00:02:01.308
Blue or black?

00:02:01.368 --> 00:02:05.689
I look at the woman on the screen.

00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:14.892
Oh — the black hat, I say. No! says Shami.
  
00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:18.194
The blue hat is nicer.

00:02:18.254 --> 00:02:22.037
We watch and wait.

00:02:22.097 --> 00:02:32.246
In the end, the woman takes the blue hat. Hurray! says Shami.
  
00:02:32.306 --> 00:02:36.989
You two know nothing about hats.

00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:38.612
Yes.

00:02:38.672 --> 00:02:43.016
It's interesting work.

00:02:43.076 --> 00:02:48.851
Today, I'm watching the screens.

00:02:48.911 --> 00:02:54.566
I'm looking at a man with a big bag.

00:02:54.626 --> 00:02:58.560
He's got a clock in his hand.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:02.833
He looks around slowly.

00:03:02.893 --> 00:03:08.766
Now, he's got a clock in his bag.

00:03:08.826 --> 00:03:12.519
The man walks to the door.

00:03:12.578 --> 00:03:15.871
I talk on my radio.

00:03:15.931 --> 00:03:21.476
Shami walks quietly behind the man.

00:03:21.536 --> 00:03:28.472
When he gets to the door, she puts her hand on his arm.

00:03:28.532 --> 00:03:34.196
Please come with me, she says.

00:03:34.256 --> 00:03:40.962
Good. I go back to the screens.

00:03:41.022 --> 00:03:47.446
And then I see her.

00:03:47.506 --> 00:03:52.798
Wow! Who's that girl?
 
00:03:52.858 --> 00:03:55.180
What girl?

00:03:55.240 --> 00:04:00.842
I can see lots of girls, Leon says.

00:04:00.902 --> 00:04:05.524
Now the picture on the screen is bigger.

00:04:05.584 --> 00:04:10.438
That girl there, with red hair.

00:04:10.498 --> 00:04:14.212
Leon looks at the screen.

00:04:14.332 --> 00:04:20.195
Hmm, yes. She's okay.
 
00:04:20.255 --> 00:04:22.696
But who is she?

00:04:22.756 --> 00:04:24.718
I don't know.

00:04:24.778 --> 00:04:30.290
Why don't you go and ask her, Mark?

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:35.282
He laughs and walks away.

00:04:35.342 --> 00:04:40.058
But I can't stop looking at the screen.

00:04:40.118 --> 00:04:43.976
Who is that beautiful girl?

00:04:44.035 --> 00:04:46.798
What is her name?

00:04:46.858 --> 00:04:51.012
I want to meet her.

00:04:51.072 --> 00:05:01.381
Every day I look for the girl with red hair, but I do not see her.

00:05:01.441 --> 00:05:04.044
Where is she?

00:05:04.104 --> 00:05:06.855
Leon says every day.

00:05:06.915 --> 00:05:11.158
Where's the girl with red hair, Mark?

00:05:11.218 --> 00:05:13.400
What's her name?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:19.672
Oh, stop it, Leon, says Shami.

00:05:19.732 --> 00:05:23.455
Mark can dream, can't he?

00:05:23.515 --> 00:05:31.450
I laugh at first, but after three days, I want to hit Leon.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:37.468
Then, suddenly, I see her again.

00:05:37.528 --> 00:05:42.544
I am watching a woman with a big bag.

00:05:42.604 --> 00:05:49.706
And then, there she is, the girl with red hair.

00:05:49.766 --> 00:05:53.778
She's got green eyes too.

00:05:53.838 --> 00:05:59.970
But there is a baby with her, a little boy.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:06.084
They are looking at a book about trains.

00:06:06.144 --> 00:06:11.120
Look, Greg, she says.

00:06:11.179 --> 00:06:14.302
Look at the big train.

00:06:14.362 --> 00:06:17.604
The little boy smiles.

00:06:17.664 --> 00:06:22.276
He's got red hair and green eyes too.

00:06:22.335 --> 00:06:24.537
Her baby.

00:06:24.597 --> 00:06:28.950
So — has she got a husband?

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:31.530
A boyfriend.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.074
I look at her beautiful green eyes again.

00:06:36.134 --> 00:06:39.707
And then I go back to work.

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:46.058
But there are lots of questions in my head.

00:06:46.118 --> 00:06:52.490
She comes to the store on Wednesday mornings.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:59.412
She usually arrives at about eleven o'clock.

00:06:59.472 --> 00:07:04.722
How's your girl? asks Leon.
 
00:07:04.782 --> 00:07:08.702
She's not my girl, I say.

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:11.644
I don't know her name.

00:07:11.704 --> 00:07:20.461
Her little boy's name is Greg, but she's the girl with red hair.

00:07:20.521 --> 00:07:27.227
Well, let's give her a name, says Leon.

00:07:27.286 --> 00:07:31.610
What do you think, Shami?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.436
Scarlett!

00:07:34.496 --> 00:07:39.801
Her name is Scarlet, says Shami.

00:07:39.861 --> 00:07:44.182
Apples are red, says Leon.

00:07:44.242 --> 00:07:47.544
Apple is a nice name.

00:07:47.604 --> 00:08:08.500
Then he looks at my face and runs out the door.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:14.200
Chapter 2. Boohoo. 

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:26.751
Next Wednesday I am in the store when the girl with red hair comes in with Greg.

00:08:26.811 --> 00:08:31.723
She stops and looks at a picture.

00:08:31.783 --> 00:08:37.497
Greg takes his hat off and drops it.

00:08:37.557 --> 00:08:43.192
I pick up the hat and go over to her.

00:08:43.252 --> 00:08:50.358
Excuse me, I say, is this your little boy's hat?

00:08:50.418 --> 00:08:53.290
She smiles at me.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:57.883
Oh, thank you, she says.

00:08:57.943 --> 00:09:02.606
Greg, look, it's your hat.

00:09:02.666 --> 00:09:05.557
Greg laughs.

00:09:05.617 --> 00:09:11.628
She puts out her hand and takes the hat from me.

00:09:11.688 --> 00:09:14.760
Is she wearing a ring?

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:20.132
No, there is no ring on her hand.

00:09:20.192 --> 00:09:27.106
Wednesday is the best day of the week, I think.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:37.548
Ten minutes later, I am near the flowers when Leon speaks to me on my radio.

00:09:37.608 --> 00:09:41.260
Mark, go to the door.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:45.612
He says, you must stop her.

00:09:45.672 --> 00:09:48.853
The girl with red hair.

00:09:48.914 --> 00:09:52.300
What? What's happening?
 
00:09:52.385 --> 00:09:56.900
I say. Go quickly — now. 

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.024
It’s the little boy —

00:10:00.084 --> 00:10:04.631
he’s got one of the red planes.

00:10:04.691 --> 00:10:07.924
Those red planes.

00:10:07.984 --> 00:10:14.279
Children take them all the time because they like the colour.

00:10:14.339 --> 00:10:19.974
Then they get to the door and the alarm rings.

00:10:20.034 --> 00:10:25.358
Children cry and their mothers get angry.

00:10:25.418 --> 00:10:29.893
I hate those planes.

00:10:29.953 --> 00:10:36.597
When I get to the door, the alarm is ringing.

00:10:36.657 --> 00:10:44.439
The girl with red hair is standing there, and her face is red.

00:10:44.499 --> 00:10:48.500
What's happening? She says.
 
00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:55.182
Please come back into the store for a minute, I say.

00:10:55.242 --> 00:11:02.258
We go back into the store, and the alarm stops.

00:11:02.318 --> 00:11:07.994
This young man has got the answer, I think.

00:11:08.054 --> 00:11:10.674
Where's the plane?

00:11:10.734 --> 00:11:13.555
I say to Greg.

00:11:13.616 --> 00:11:18.758
Plane. Says Greg.
 
00:11:18.818 --> 00:11:24.190
And he waves a little red plane at us.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:29.111
Oh, I am sorry, she says.

00:11:29.171 --> 00:11:32.528
It's all right, I say.

00:11:32.588 --> 00:11:35.796
It happens all the time.

00:11:35.856 --> 00:11:38.778
Can I have the plane?

00:11:38.838 --> 00:11:41.238
Good boy.

00:11:41.298 --> 00:11:43.930
Thank you very much.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.872
Says the girl with red hair.

00:11:46.932 --> 00:11:50.524
But the alarm is ringing again.

00:11:50.584 --> 00:11:53.845
I must go.

00:11:53.905 --> 00:11:59.268
I walk into the office upstairs.

00:11:59.328 --> 00:12:03.200
Shami is watching the screens.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:08.044
She stops and looks at my face.

00:12:08.103 --> 00:12:13.328
She says nothing, but she smiles.

00:12:13.388 --> 00:12:17.450
Then she goes back to work.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:25.586
I look at the screens too, but I am dreaming.

00:12:25.646 --> 00:12:31.813
I'm happy. I'm really happy.
 
00:12:31.873 --> 00:12:36.038
But how can I meet her again?

00:12:36.098 --> 00:12:40.890
I think about this for the next six days.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:45.022
But I can't find any answers.

00:12:45.082 --> 00:12:49.565
Then it's Wednesday again.

00:12:49.624 --> 00:12:54.500
I'm sitting in the office watching the screens.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:59.389
10 o'clock comes and goes.

00:12:59.449 --> 00:13:02.046
Then 11 o'clock.

00:13:02.106 --> 00:13:06.424
I can't see her.

00:13:06.484 --> 00:13:12.658
I look on every screen in the store.

00:13:12.718 --> 00:13:18.042
In the end, I see her near the door.

00:13:18.102 --> 00:13:24.517
She's looking at her watch and talking to Greg.

00:13:24.576 --> 00:13:28.390
Is she waiting for somebody?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.856
Perhaps she's meeting somebody.

00:13:32.916 --> 00:13:35.892
Perhaps she's late.

00:13:35.952 --> 00:13:39.754
Perhaps her mother is coming.

00:13:39.814 --> 00:13:41.986
Perhaps.

00:13:42.046 --> 00:13:47.240
But now she's waving at somebody.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:57.666
A good-looking man in a black jacket walks up to the girl with red hair and kisses her.

00:13:57.726 --> 00:14:05.689
Greg laughs and the man picks him up and kisses him too.

00:14:05.749 --> 00:14:09.032
Is he the baby's father?

00:14:09.092 --> 00:14:11.974
Of course he is.

00:14:12.034 --> 00:14:14.936
Anybody can see that.

00:14:14.996 --> 00:14:17.588
I don't want to look.

00:14:17.648 --> 00:14:22.652
But I can't take my eyes away from the screen.

00:14:22.712 --> 00:14:28.828
Then they all go down the road, away from the store.

00:14:28.887 --> 00:14:31.818
I look around the room.

00:14:31.878 --> 00:14:39.522
Leon and Shami are in the store and the room is very quiet.

00:14:39.582 --> 00:14:43.924
It feels cold.

00:14:43.984 --> 00:14:49.637
Then Leon and Shami come in.

00:14:49.698 --> 00:14:53.560
Now that's not a happy face.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:57.382
Shami says, what's the matter?

00:14:57.442 --> 00:14:59.234
I tell them.

00:14:59.294 --> 00:15:02.688
I tell them about the girl with red hair.

00:15:02.748 --> 00:15:08.602
and Greg, and the good-looking man, and the kiss.

00:15:08.661 --> 00:15:13.854
Leon looks at my face and thinks for a minute.

00:15:13.914 --> 00:15:20.317
Look Mark, he says, it's a dream, that's all.

00:15:20.377 --> 00:15:27.500
You see a nice girl, you think about her, you talk to her, 

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:31.594
and one day her boyfriend arrives.

00:15:31.654 --> 00:15:36.798
Boo hoo, you stop dreaming.

00:15:36.858 --> 00:15:43.060
But there are always more girls.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:50.194
Yes, but I say, and then I stop.

00:15:50.254 --> 00:15:55.676
But they're not the girl with red hair, right?

00:15:55.736 --> 00:15:57.446
Says Leon.

00:15:57.507 --> 00:16:01.105
But she's got a boyfriend.

00:16:01.165 --> 00:16:04.434
You need a different girl, Mark.

00:16:04.494 --> 00:16:08.096
A girl without a boyfriend.

00:16:08.156 --> 00:16:11.748
Why don't you come out with us tonight?

00:16:11.808 --> 00:16:15.079
We're going to Ocean Blue.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:21.834
It's a wonderful club, and there are lots of nice girls there.

00:16:21.894 --> 00:16:28.984
I don't really want to go, but I don't want to stay at home and do nothing.

00:16:29.044 --> 00:16:36.172
Okay then, I say, good man, says Leon.

00:16:36.232 --> 00:16:53.100
See you there at 9.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:58.500
Chapter 3. Yay!!
 
00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.646
The club is dark.

00:17:01.706 --> 00:17:09.860
There's a lot of noise and a lot of people, but the music is good.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:14.642
Leon is there with his girlfriend Ellie.

00:17:14.701 --> 00:17:18.494
I talk to them and their friends.

00:17:18.554 --> 00:17:21.054
I'm feeling good.

00:17:21.115 --> 00:17:26.386
Perhaps tonight I can forget about everything.

00:17:26.446 --> 00:17:29.529
Leon and Ellie are dancing.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:33.702
So I go to get a drink.

00:17:33.762 --> 00:17:38.714
Leon is right about one thing.

00:17:38.774 --> 00:17:44.136
There are a lot of nice girls at Ocean Blue.

00:17:44.196 --> 00:17:55.011
Tall girls, interesting girls, girls with black hair, blue hair, and red hair.

00:17:55.071 --> 00:17:57.162
Red hair?

00:17:57.222 --> 00:17:59.500
I'm waiting for my drink.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:04.776
and I'm standing next to the girl with red hair.

00:18:04.836 --> 00:18:09.380
No, two girls with red hair.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:13.632
Is this really happening?

00:18:13.692 --> 00:18:20.256
The girl with red hair looks at me and smiles.

00:18:20.316 --> 00:18:26.158
Just a minute, she says, don't I know you?

00:18:26.219 --> 00:18:28.750
She's talking to me.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:32.203
Why can't I say anything?

00:18:32.263 --> 00:18:36.546
In the store, I say at last.

00:18:36.606 --> 00:18:44.300
In Mason's store, with your little boy, and the red plane, 

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:48.100
the girl with red hair laughs.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:58.950
Oh, with Greg, she says, I remember, but he isn't my baby.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:00.938
He's Claire's.

00:19:00.998 --> 00:19:04.628
This is my sister Claire.

00:19:04.688 --> 00:19:06.779
She's his mother.

00:19:06.839 --> 00:19:12.562
The second girl with red hair waves at me.

00:19:12.622 --> 00:19:19.114
But I always see you with him, I say.

00:19:19.174 --> 00:19:28.204
I look after Greg on Wednesday mornings and we always go to Mason's, she says.

00:19:28.264 --> 00:19:31.102
Then I meet Claire.

00:19:31.163 --> 00:19:37.634
Well, usually that is, but not this week.

00:19:37.694 --> 00:19:44.245
Just then, a good-looking man in a black jacket arrives.

00:19:44.305 --> 00:19:50.016
Sorry I'm late, he says, and kisses Claire.

00:19:50.076 --> 00:19:51.907
Hi Kate.

00:19:51.967 --> 00:19:58.298
Claire smiles at him, and the girl with red hair says hello.

00:19:58.358 --> 00:20:02.038
I'm starting to understand.

00:20:02.098 --> 00:20:07.690
This is Claire's husband and Greg's father.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:14.010
And the girl with red hair is called Kate.

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:18.852
My face is red.

00:20:18.912 --> 00:20:23.943
Hey, I'm sorry, I say to Kate.

00:20:24.003 --> 00:20:30.836
It's, well, Greg's got your hair and your eyes.

00:20:30.896 --> 00:20:33.827
But I can see now.

00:20:33.887 --> 00:20:37.368
He's got Claire's hair and eyes.

00:20:37.428 --> 00:20:42.282
Of course. It's okay, Kate says.
 
00:20:42.342 --> 00:20:44.572
It happens all the time.

00:20:44.633 --> 00:20:49.476
People say, isn't your little boy happy?

00:20:49.536 --> 00:20:56.378
And sometimes I just say, yes, he is.

00:20:56.438 --> 00:21:05.252
Claire and her husband go off to dance, and I get Kate a drink.

00:21:05.312 --> 00:21:07.474
Here you are, Kate.

00:21:07.534 --> 00:21:09.836
My name's Mark.

00:21:09.896 --> 00:21:11.676
Thanks, Mark.

00:21:11.736 --> 00:21:17.050
She says, so you work in Mason's.

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:22.443
Yes, I say, I work in security.

00:21:22.504 --> 00:21:26.582
I look for little boys with red planes.

00:21:26.642 --> 00:21:29.859
and girls with red hair.

00:21:29.919 --> 00:21:33.060
And do you find them?

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:39.392
I find lots of little boys with red planes.

00:21:39.452 --> 00:21:43.134
And the girls?

00:21:43.194 --> 00:21:45.605
Just one.

00:21:45.665 --> 00:21:50.416
Now I have the answers to my questions.

00:21:50.476 --> 00:21:54.140
The girl with red hair is Kate.

00:21:54.200 --> 00:22:00.278
She hasn't got a husband and she hasn't got a baby.

00:22:00.338 --> 00:22:05.754
And those green eyes are smiling at me.

00:22:05.814 --> 00:22:13.000
Yes, Wednesday really is the best day of the week.